{
  "change": "Prevent unrelated forms from consuming one another\u2019s attempt budgets",
  "date": "2026-10-17",
  "root_cause": "Default numeric Laravel throttle signatures used a shared guest domain/IP key across routes; custom bearer authentication was not included in the default Laravel user resolver. Login and other form traffic could therefore exhaust MFA\u2019s smaller budget.",
  "implementation": [
    "All 66 numeric route rules now use action-template/method plus verified account identity or public IP scope",
    "Authentication and network admission run before account-scoped throttling; raw bearer values, query parameters and concrete record IDs cannot create fresh buckets",
    "Existing route numeric limits, per-tenant service quotas, global 300-request/minute network guard, device binding, role checks, TOTP replay control and 15-minute privileged MFA freshness preserved",
    "HEAD requests share GET action scope",
    "Scoped 429 responses include exact Retry-After, no-store and structured retry_after; AtomicQuota includes actual current window retry time",
    "Shared API response parser turns generic 429 responses into actionable wait messages, including proxy HTML responses",
    "MFA disables retry during server-issued wait, recomputes elapsed time after tab suspension/focus and automatically re-enables without resubmitting codes"
  ],
